--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PREAMBLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project is released in the spirit of the Hardware Liberation Army:

    We have put up with locked-down hardware that we don't own for long enough.
    Hardware with software so locked-down, subscription-bound, or dumpster-bound
    that the effort to open it never seemed worth it. No more.

    Our goal is interoperability and our own hardware back: to read our own
    recordings, to use our own devices, to stop paying rent on things we bought,
    and to turn would-be e-waste back into tools we control.

This license exists so that reverse-engineered protocols and the tools that
implement them can be shared, studied, and improved by anyone - and so that
the work of opening up hardware is never again gated behind effort that isn't
"worth it."

